1
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:10,240
China is one of the world's most fascinating and complicated countries,

2
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:14,440
and its cities seem to get bigger every year.

3
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:23,440
Considered a rural society just a few decades ago,

4
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:28,640
China today is home to the world's largest urban population.

5
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:39,360
I traveled to China independently for more than a decade,
on several occasions.

6
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:47,040
And in this video I will show you some of the most striking
and interesting cities I came across.

7
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:56,080
From the ancient centers of Beijing and Xian,

8
00:00:57,360 --> 00:01:01,400
to the modern megacities of Shenzhen and Guangzhou.

9
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:09,880
We visit the freezing Winter festivals of Harbin

10
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:16,280
and the popular Summer holiday beaches of coastal Qingdao.

11
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:27,920
From the streets of fusion cities like Hong Kong and Macau,
we travel to Tibetan Lhasa,

12
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:31,640
located on the 'Rooftop of the World'.

13
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:44,720
We also take a look at the now historic alleys of Kashgar,
in the controversial Xinjiang province,

14
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:53,240
and the empty streets of Ordos, China's best known 'ghost town'.

15
00:01:55,360 --> 00:02:00,040
And we explore the expanding urban centers along the Yangtze river,

16
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:04,080
all the way to the fast paced metropolis of Shanghai.

17
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:10,120
So join me on this journey through urban China.

18
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:32,880
We begin our travels in Shanghai, one of China's most
unique and dynamic cities.

19
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:41,400
Its iconic skyline has become a symbol of the country's
explosive economic growth of the past decades,

20
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:46,400
and provides a glimpse into the many changes China has undergone.

21
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:53,800
While it's a lot of glitz, glamour, and commerce here,

22
00:02:53,800 --> 00:03:02,040
Shanghai also has some beautiful historic architecture,
peaceful parks and laidback neighborhoods.

23
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:09,240
Most travelers start their trip to Shanghai on the Bund,

24
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:16,480
a waterfront promenade lined with former Western
consulates and financial institutions.

25
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:23,320
Many of these buildings are now used as restaurants,
bars and fashion stores,

26
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:31,960
and are a stunning contrast with the modern skyline of Pudong,
Shanghai's business district.

27
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:47,320
Most farmland only 3 decades ago, this spectacle of skyscrapers
has become a major financial hub.

28
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:59,760
Some of the buildings have observation decks,
from where you can get amazing views over the city.

29
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:13,760
For those interested in China's economic story, 
it may be worthwhile to hire a taxi

30
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:19,440
to the city's water port, the largest container terminal in the world.

31
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:43,240
Shanghai is a city of commerce, which is best seen
by walking Nanjing Lu,

32
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:48,040
a pedestrian only shopping street in the heart of the city.

33
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:03,800
If the crowds become overwhelming, the nearby Jing'An temple
might bring some relief,

34
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:12,000
where you can join a Buddhist ceremony, or simply escape
the hustle and bustle from the streets.

35
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:32,600
More traditional neighborhoods still exist, but you 
have to look closely these days to find them.

36
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:42,280
Walking some of the narrow alleyways of this old Shanghai
is an adventure on its own,

37
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:47,240
and it's easy to get lost both in time and place.

38
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:16,960
This authentic Shanghai, however, is disappearing fast,
as many buildings are taken down,

39
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:21,040
and replaced by apartment towers and shopping malls.

40
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:39,520
Whatever you think of it, this is the story of Shanghai, 
a city in constant flux, changing all the time. 

41
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:46,040
And who dares to guess what it will look like in a few decades?

42
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:05,200
After Shanghai, we travel all the way North of China,
to visit Harbin,

43
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:12,280
a city of over 5 million people, with a strong historic Russian influence.

44
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:21,080
While it's a good place to visit all year, things really get busy in Winter,

45
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:27,160
when millions of people come to see the famous 
Ice and Snow festival.

46
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:44,280
Thousands of workers prepare for many weeks in
bitterly cold conditions,

47
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:45,280
building temples, sculptures and palaces, all made from ice and snow.

48
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:59,040
Watching them at work may be as impressive as the festival itself.

49
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:22,600
Other than admiring the craftsmanship and artwork,
visitors can also take part in many Winter activities.

50
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:30,680
And as you walk around the festival grounds, you will see people
sledding, skating, and using ice bicycles.

51
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:55,400
While spectacular during the day, my favorite time to visit
the festival was around sunset.

52
00:08:56,480 --> 00:09:05,400
At twilight, the ice sculptures are lit up with beautiful neon lights,
creating a magical atmosphere.

53
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:11,280
Temperatures also drop dramatically, so be sure to wear enough layers.

54
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:38,360
We travel onwards to Beijing, the nation's capital.

55
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:44,280
Beijing has a history that goes back more than 3,000 years.

56
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:50,880
It's the polical center of China, but also brims with culture and creativity.

57
00:09:53,240 --> 00:09:57,520
A good place to start exploring the city is Tiananmen Square,

58
00:09:57,520 --> 00:10:03,000
where Mao Zedong proclaimed the People's Republic of China, in 1949,

59
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:06,840
an event that changed the course of the country drastically.

60
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:17,640
Since then, Tiananmen has been used for celebrations and parades,

61
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:24,520
but was also the epicenter of a suppressed student protest in 1989.

62
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:36,120
These days, the square is a hotspot for Chinese tourists,
and gets especially busy on national holidays. 

63
00:10:53,120 --> 00:11:01,320
Across from Tiananmen lies the Forbidden City, one of the
most interesting historical sites in Beijing.

64
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:11,960
Off limits for 500 years, hence its name, this is the largest and
best preserved cluster of ancient buildings in China.

65
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:22,840
Two dynasties of Emperors lived here, who only left the 
walled city when they really had to.

66
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:32,600
Other landmarks in Beijing include the Summer Palace, 
and the Temple of Heaven Park,

67
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:37,320
a beautiful complex of religious buildings in the South of the city. 

68
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:44,840
Watching some of the daily life in the parks,
and some of the remaining 'hutongs',

69
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:51,040
narrow alleyways in traditional neighborhoods, is one of 
the best things you can do in Beijing.

70
00:11:53,560 --> 00:12:00,320
You might come across people playing 'jianzi', best described
as a mix of badminton and football,

71
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:04,520
or people playing 'mahjong', the classic Chinese tile game.

72
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:14,440
Don't leave the city without tasting, or at least smelling, Peking Duck,
a dish first served to emperors.

73
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:17,720
and watching a show of Beijing opera.

74
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:43,040
Beijing also had a modern face, which you will meet 
as you travel through the city.

75
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:50,240
Head to Wangfujing, to get a sense of the commercial face of Beijing,

76
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:56,720
or take a look at the impressive stadiums, inside 
the 2008 OIympics park.

77
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:14,440
A must do when in Beijing, is visit the Great Wall,

78
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:23,280
a series of fortifications that were built along the borders of 
ancient Chinese states, and later imperial China.

79
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:31,880
These stretches were linked when China was unified in the Qing Dynasty, more than 2,000 years ago,

80
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:35,840
and became known as the Great Wall of China.

81
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:52,840
Now, the people you see climbing the Wall here can actually not watch this video.

82
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:55,840
Their internet access is restricted by the Chinese government,

83
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:58,840
something that is often referred to as the 'Great Firewall of China'.

84
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:06,640
Many foreign websites and apps are blocked, including Facebook, Instagram, Google, and also Youtube.

85
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:12,720
Aside from the impact on Chinese society, this can also be very inconvenient for travelers,

86
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:15,000
something I experienced first hand.

87
